Here is a thorough breakdown of the `siarhei-luskanau/compose-multiplatform-template` repository.

---

## 1. Module Structure

The project uses `TYPESAFE_PROJECT_ACCESSORS` and includes 11 Gradle modules (plus 1 convention-plugin build):

```
settings.gradle.kts includes:
  :app:androidApp
  :app:desktopApp
  :app:webApp
  :composeApp
  :core:coreCommon
  :core:corePref
  :navigation
  :ui:uiCommon
  :ui:uiMain
  :ui:uiSplash
```

**Plus the convention plugin included via `includeBuild`:**
```
convention-plugin-multiplatform   (included build, not a module)
```

**Also present but NOT in settings.gradle.kts:**
```
app/iosApp   (native Swift/Xcode project, referenced outside Gradle)
```

### Module Purposes

| Module | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `:composeApp` | Shared multiplatform library — wires all other modules, contains `KoinApp.kt` (Koin initialization + root `NavApp()` composable) |
| `:core:coreCommon` | Cross-platform utilities: `DispatcherSet` interface, `PlatformService`, `CoreCommonModule` (expect/actual) |
| `:core:corePref` | Preference storage abstraction: `PrefService` interface, `PrefData` data class, platform-specific DataStore (Android/iOS/JVM) and memory (web) implementations |
| `:navigation` | Navigation graph: `NavApp.kt` composable (Navigation3 `NavDisplay`), `AppNavigation.kt` back-stack manager, `AppRoutes` sealed interface |
| `:ui:uiCommon` | Shared Compose resources (icons, strings, etc.) — `publicResClass = true` |
| `:ui:uiMain` | Main screen composable + `MainViewModel` |
| `:ui:uiSplash` | Splash screen composable + `SplashViewModel` |
| `:app:androidApp` | Android `Application` entry point — `AppActivity` extends `ComponentActivity`, calls `KoinApp()` |
| `:app:desktopApp` | JVM desktop entry point — `main()` function in `MainKt`, produces DMG/MSI/DEB |
| `:app:webApp` | JS + WasmJs browser targets |

---

## 2. build.gradle.kts Structure Per Module

### Convention Plugin — `composeMultiplatformConvention.gradle.kts`

This is the heart of the build. All shared library modules apply `id("composeMultiplatformConvention")`.

```kotlin
// convention-plugin-multiplatform/src/main/kotlin/composeMultiplatformConvention.gradle.kts

import org.gradle.accessors.dm.LibrariesForLibs
import org.jetbrains.kotlin.gradle.plugin.mpp.KotlinNativeTarget

val libs = the<LibrariesForLibs>()

plugins {
    id("com.android.kotlin.multiplatform.library")
    kotlin("multiplatform")
    id("org.jetbrains.compose")
    kotlin("plugin.compose")
}

kotlin {
    jvmToolchain(libs.versions.javaVersion.get().toInt())
    compilerOptions { freeCompilerArgs.add("-Xexplicit-backing-fields") }

    androidLibrary {
        compileSdk = libs.versions.build.android.compileSdk.get().toInt()
        minSdk = libs.versions.build.android.minSdk.get().toInt()
        androidResources.enable = true
        withHostTestBuilder {}.configure {
            isIncludeAndroidResources = true
            enableCoverage = true
        }
        packaging.resources.excludes.add("META-INF/**")
    }

    jvm()
    js { browser() }
    wasmJs { browser() }
    iosArm64()
    iosSimulatorArm64()

    sourceSets {
        commonMain.dependencies {
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.animation)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.animation.graphics)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.components.resources)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.foundation)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.material3)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.runtime)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.ui)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.ui.tooling.preview)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.lifecycle.viewmodel.navigation3)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.savedstate.compose)
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.window.core)
            implementation(libs.koin.compose)
            implementation(libs.kotlinx.coroutines.core)
            implementation(project.dependencies.platform(libs.koin.bom))
        }
        commonTest.dependencies {
            implementation(libs.jetbrains.compose.ui.test)
            implementation(kotlin("test"))
        }
        jvmMain.dependencies {
            implementation(compose.desktop.currentOs)
            implementation(libs.kotlinx.coroutines.swing)
        }
    }

    targets.withType<KotlinNativeTarget>()
        .matching { it.konanTarget.family.isAppleFamily }
        .configureEach { binaries { framework { baseName = "ComposeApp" } } }
}

tasks.withType<Test>().matching { it.name.contains("AndroidHostTest") }.configureEach {
    exclude("**/*CommonTest*")
}
tasks.withType<AbstractTestTask>().configureEach { failOnNoDiscoveredTests = false }
```

Key facts:
- Plugin ID `"com.android.kotlin.multiplatform.library"` — AGP's new multiplatform library plugin (not `com.android.library`)
- Targets: `androidLibrary`, `jvm()`, `js { browser() }`, `wasmJs { browser() }`, `iosArm64()`, `iosSimulatorArm64()`
- iOS binaries produce a framework named `"ComposeApp"`
- No `iosX64()` — simulator uses `iosSimulatorArm64` only

